    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        418,
        185,
        470,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": 169,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "You have already learnt how verbs with a first aorist form their aorist participle on the first aorist stem. Verbs with a second aorist form it (hard to believe though it is) on the second aorist stem.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 1,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        488,
        185,
        503,
        387
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Second aorist stems",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        513,
        185,
        565,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "You are already familiar with how to form the first aorist stem (131ff.): take the aorist indicative, and remove (i) the augment and (ii) the personal endings. As you have seen, it works for second aorists as follows (144ff.):",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 2,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        579,
        237,
        650,
        680
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἔ-λαβ-ον\naorist stem: λαβ-\nἦλθ-ον\naorist stem: ἐλθ-\nἐ-γεν-όμην\naorist stem: γεν-\nἀπ-ἐ-φυγ-ον\naorist stem: ἀποφυγ-",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        666,
